<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="34210" href="schedule/2022/fall/HIST/422/34210.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2022" href="schedule/2022.xml">2022</calendarYear><term id="120228" href="schedule/2022/fall.xml">Fall 2022</term><subject id="HIST" href="schedule/2022/fall/HIST.xml">History</subject><course id="422" href="schedule/2022/fall/HIST/422.xml">Soc-Econ Hist Modern China</course></parents><sectionNumber>U3 </sectionNumber><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic:  China-United States Relations  Description:  This course follows two parallel and intertwined narratives: China's century-long struggle to find its place in the world and China's relations with the United States. The course emphasizes key moments in the trans-Pacific relationship such as the Sino-American alliance against Japan, the "loss" of China and the Korean war, and a legendary ping-pong match that some say, "changed the World."</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>CrossListOpen (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2022-08-22Z</startDate><endDate>2022-12-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>12:30 PM</start><end>01:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>307</roomNumber><buildingName>Gregory Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Fu" firstName="P">Fu, P</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>